<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Voivodeship of Litovoi</h1><p class="st-meta">1247 CE – 1279 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Romanian voivodeship west of the Olt whose ruler died fighting Hungary around 1279, an early step towards an independent Wallachia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litovoi">Litovoi's</a> land appears in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bela-iv-of-hungary">Béla IV</a>'s charter of 1247 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>, which names a knezate of Litovoi in the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiu-river">Jiu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olt-river">Olt</a>, possibly including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hateg-country">Hațeg</a> country across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litovoi">Litovoi</a> ruled Romanian knezes as a Hungarian tributary. A royal charter of 1285 says that around 1277–1279 a voivode Litovoi, with his brothers, seized part of the kingdom and refused to pay tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A Hungarian force under Master George defeated the rebels: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litovoi">Litovoi</a> was killed and his brother Bărbat captured and forced to pay a large ransom. The land later became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-wallachia">Principality of Wallachia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basarab-i">Basarab I</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1247 CE – 1279 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.52%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1247 CE – 1279 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Litovoi, Bărbat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Litovoi's voivodeship, Knezate of Litovoi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1263&amp;focus=voivodeship-of-litovoi" aria-label="Voivodeship of Litovoi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5277 583 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Voivodeship of Litovoi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5446 783h0M5624 862h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5597 839h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5597 839h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=1263&amp;focus=voivodeship-of-litovoi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
